Hello,

I am following up on the confidential QEMU security report that I submitted
through GitLab:

https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu/-/work_items/4088

The report concerns a potential guest-to-host escape vulnerability that may
result in code execution in the context of the QEMU process.

I understand that the QEMU project cannot guarantee a specific response
time for security reports. However, since I have not yet received an
acknowledgement, I would appreciate it if you could confirm whether the
report is visible to the appropriate maintainers and has been placed in the
security triage queue.

I have validated the issue and can provide additional information if
necessary, including:

   -

   Affected QEMU versions and commits
   -

   Reproduction environment and command line
   -

   Proof of concept
   -

   Debugger and sanitizer logs
   -

   Root-cause analysis
   -

   A proposed mitigation or patch

Because this is a security-sensitive issue, I have intentionally omitted
the technical details from this email. I would prefer to continue all
technical discussion through the confidential GitLab work item.

Please let me know if any additional information is required for triage.

Best regards,

Taeyong Kim
GitLab username: [TaeD]
Contact: [kty0730wq@yonsei.ac.kr]

